<h3 class=3D"text-lg font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-1.5">=F0=9F=92=AD Fin=
al Thoughts from a Principal's Perspective</h3>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">After building web applications =
at companies like NAB, Axon, Binance, Webflow, and Figma, I've learned that=
 <strong>DOM mastery separates good engineers from great ones</strong>. It'=
s the foundation that everything else builds upon.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">When you truly understand DOM na=
vigation:</p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>React patterns</strong>=
 make more sense</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Performance debugging</=
strong> becomes intuitive</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Architecture decisions<=
/strong> are better informed</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Code reviews</strong> s=
pot issues others miss</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Technical discussions</=
strong> carry more weight</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>The DOM is not just an A=
PI - it's the interface between your logic and the user's experience.</stro=
ng> Master it, and you master web development.</p>
